From: Michael R Sweet <msweet@msweet.org>
Date: Fri, 15 Nov 2024 11:55:07 -0500
Subject: Fix make-and-model whitespace trimming (Issue #1096)

The trailing-whitespace loop that came with the CVE-2024-47175 hardening
(0014) does not stop at the first non-space character, so it replaces every
space in printer-make-and-model with a NUL. Generated IPP Everywhere PPDs
then use only the first word as the make and "Printer" as the model, e.g.
"Printer - IPP Everywhere" instead of "G3010 series - IPP Everywhere".

Origin: upstream, https://github.com/OpenPrinting/cups/commit/5cc470c8d95df40f32e8a401b2946886c91b03d1
Bug: https://github.com/OpenPrinting/cups/issues/1096
Applied-Upstream: 2.4.12
Last-Update: 2026-10-25
---
 cups/ppd-cache.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/cups/ppd-cache.c
+++ b/cups/ppd-cache.c
@@ -3294,6 +3294,8 @@
       mptr --;
       if (*mptr == ' ')
 	*mptr = '\0';
+      else
+        break;
     }

     if (!make[0])
